tps://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":656,"digest":"sha256:732e311dee247553b6a21c8f2eb4911b25bf6d49fa0ba955b678e60c9ed76100","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T22:47:45Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T22:47:46Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m1313-v0.13.13/m13stage13-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m1313-v0.13.13","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m1313-v0.13.13","body":"# Engacer OS M13.13 / 0.13.13\n\n**Development release - owner-revised stability scope.** The owner explicitly accepted ninety minutes instead of the original eight-hour requirement. The frozen candidate reached **6,526.844 actual observed seconds (108.78 minutes)**. Its original eight-hour/two-hour idle report was stopped at owner direction and remains incomplete; neither original gate is claimed passed. The host-laptop explanation is an owner report, not an independently established cause.\n\n## Download and install\n\nUse the matching ISO or extract the entire new blank-disk VMware ZIP. The prepared starter includes a growable 20-GiB SATA disk, two CPUs, 128 MiB RAM, UEFI and Secure Boot off, with all shipped devices enabled. It is not preinstalled. Follow the [eight-step installation guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/48585b41acbc1627800f34d09bb198f214495440/docs/handbook/install-m1313.md), [first-day guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/48585b41acbc1627800f34d09bb198f214495440/docs/handbook/final-m1313.md) and [saved-work/stability guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/48585b41acbc1627800f34d09bb198f214495440/docs/handbook/stability-m1313.md).\n\nBuild: `49a6fe1047488276f64b7d12433c0113`. ISO SHA-256: `41c0fe24841a01d4e8920dd184609fcd9aad0d74ce30eb5cc3bdcd65c27ddef2`. VMware ZIP SHA-256: `c1c1df9523fd8fd7ebf517a4be32c344dfcd3ba27cc74e14fc81d32b68bb8854`. Twenty assets include the matching media, manifests, binaries/maps, notices and corresponding third-party source/license files, with complete SHA-256 checksums.\n\n## Exact scope\n\nThe long frozen enabled-device VMware observation retains its original report and actual visible captures. Independent image hashes, progressing clock and unchanged dirty text support the revised observation scope. Its early stop does not provide a completed two-hour interval summary or final native session log. Separate fresh exact-candidate functional tasks complete actual installation, retained-ISO startup, file navigation/paging, context menus, window movement/resizing, Settings search/preview/cancel/apply, app launches, explicit saved-data readback, two independent disk-only starts and stopped-image data/CRC inspection. The diagnostic functional report remains diagnostic; it is not relabelled as a duration pass.\n\nSeparate constrained 1024x768/128-MiB and physical 3840x2160/1024-MiB native tasks each include three actual five-minute idle cycles, retained saved/dirty text, ordinary input after idle and independent data starts. Screensaver checks cover actual activation/wake and disabled state, persisted choices, seven malformed records and a readable declared write-refusal/cancel route. A separate exact VMware task verifies visible Preview/wake and ordinary startup. Labelled simulated display-timeout recovery passes visible operation and three warm resets; it does not reproduce or establish the cause of the historical natural freeze/reset chain.\n\n[Acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/48585b41acbc1627800f34d09bb198f214495440/evidence/M13/13/acceptance-results.json), [resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/48585b41acbc1627800f34d09bb198f214495440/evidence/M13/13/resources.json), [owner scope](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/48585b41acbc1627800f34d09bb198f214495440/evidence/M13/13/owner-duration-scope.json), [implementation and decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/48585b41acbc1627800f34d09bb198f214495440/docs/milestones/m13-13.md), [source delta](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/48585b41acbc1627800f34d09bb198f214495440/evidence/M13/13/native-source-delta.json).\n\n## Resources and limits\n\nNative implementation is unchanged from M13.12; only release identity and stage admission differ among the 613 compiled inputs. Fixed desktop state remains 557,516 bytes, installer state 48,412 bytes and font masks 251,248 bytes. Measured completed tasks retain zero managed bytes/pages and add no allocation refusals beyond the recorded boot baseline. Peak, retained state, code, configured guest RAM and framebuffer/shadow costs are separate. No extra worker, cache or idle polling loop is added.\n\nM13.12's fourteen-controller integration matrix and original supported 7-Zip console MSI lifecycle remain historical qualification of M13.12, not repeated M13.13 matrix/MSI tests. Current native source identity does not turn historical media results into new-media tests. This release does not promise universal stability, unlimited uptime, every VM configuration, physical/ARM support, vendor GPU 3D, arbitrary MSI or general DOS/Windows compatibility. Agent scenarios and visual review are not a human novice study. Keep backups; unsaved work is not promised after reset.\n\nM13.0-M13.13 closes within its recorded and explicitly revised scopes. Hardware recognition is the next development priority. Matching actual website delivery and independently downloaded public assets close separately after release publication.\n\nOriginal project code remains MIT licensed. Included third-party components retain their own notices, licenses and corresponding source assets.\n"}